# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in your key:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Never commit a real key.
# Get one at https://platform.claude.com/settings/keys

ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...

# ── Stripe (optional) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# All three, or none. With any one missing, the results page keeps saying
# "Checkout is not connected yet" and /stripe/webhook 404s — there is no
# half-live state, because a secret key without a webhook secret would take
# money and never grant access.
#
#   STRIPE_SECRET_KEY     sk_test_... from https://dashboard.stripe.com/apikeys
#   STRIPE_PRICE_ID       price_... for the $29/mo recurring price
#   STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET whsec_... printed by `stripe listen` or the dashboard
#
# The webhook endpoint is POST /stripe/webhook, and it MUST be subscribed to:
#
#   customer.subscription.created
#   customer.subscription.updated
#   customer.subscription.deleted
#
# `checkout.session.completed` alone is not enough and is the easy mistake:
# the session says a payment succeeded but carries no period end, and access
# hangs entirely on that date (see SubscriptionStore.isActive). Enable only
# that one and every customer pays and stays locked out — F21, arriving by
# configuration instead of by a dropped webhook. `npm run reconcile` repairs it
# within a day either way.
#
# Full walkthrough: docs/stripe-runbook.md. Then `npm run stripe:check`.
#
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_test_...
# STRIPE_PRICE_ID=price_...
# STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=whsec_...

# Where Stripe sends the customer back to. Defaults to http://localhost:PORT.
# USABILITY_LAB_BASE_URL=https://theusabilitylab.example
